[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 968,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 733,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137001,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 733,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Conjunctival oncocytoma is a benign neoplasm composed of columnar eosinophilic cells with numerous mitochondria (oncocytes).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:57:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 969,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 734,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137002,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 734,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8290/0 Conjunctival oncocytoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:57:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 970,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 735,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137003,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 735,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F36.Y &amp; XH9Z86 Other specified benign neoplasm of eye or ocular adnexa &amp; Oxyphilic adenoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:57:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 971,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 736,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137004,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 736,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> oncocytic adenoma; oxyphilic adenoma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> oxyphilic granular cell adenoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:57:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 972,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 737,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137005,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 737,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:57:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 973,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 738,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137006,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 738,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Periocular oncocytomas occur mostly at the caruncle, and rarely at the bulbar conjunctiva or plica semilunaris. They may also occur in the lacrimal gland (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/65/134\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Lacrimal gland oncocytoma</em>), lacrimal sac, or lid margin, or peripunctally {19843013;21956543}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:57:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 974,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 739,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137007,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 739,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Oncocytoma appears as a smooth or slightly papillomatous, circumscribed, sometimes vascularized, reddish, bluish, brownish, or (rarely) greyish or whitish nodule.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:57:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 975,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 740,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137008,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 740,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Oncocytoma is diagnosed in elderly patients and represents 2&ndash;7% of benign caruncle tumours {27725148;18927596}. The incidence is estimated to be as high as 0.3&nbsp;cases per 1&nbsp;million person-years. Differing results are found in the literature regarding sex predisposition: there was none in a study of 15&nbsp;US cases {21956543}, while in Denmark an M:F&nbsp;ratio of 1:2 was found in an investigation of 34&nbsp;cases {19843013}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:57:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 976,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 741,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137009,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 741,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:57:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 977,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 742,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137010,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 742,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Oncocytomas arise as a benign proliferation of oncocytes, the cause of which is unknown. Caruncular oncocytomas most probably originate from accessory lacrimal glands of Popoff {19843013} or sweat glands {19032382}. Lacrimal sac oncocytomas arise in seromucinous glands. Accessory lacrimal gland oncocytoma was found to harbour mitochondrial DNA mutations {21555623}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:57:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 984,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 749,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137011,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 749,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Macroscopically, oncocytoma is an ovoid, solid, sometimes cystic red-brown tumour {21956543}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:57:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 978,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 743,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137012,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 743,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Oncocytomas are subepithelial circumscribed neoplasms composed of oncocytes, which are columnar epithelial cells with abundant eosinophilic granular cytoplasm and monomorphic, ovoid, centrally placed nuclei with a single nucleolus. Neoplastic cells are typically arranged in sheets, nests, and microcystic patterns containing lumina with PAS-positive proteinaceous fluid. Some tumours demonstrate a cystadenomatous architecture with papillary projections into the lumen containing granular, eosinophilic, PAS-positive material. Scattered goblet cells may be present {3025880}.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>The tumour cells stain positively for antimitochondrial MU213-UC antibodies {19843013}. The immunohistochemical (cytokeratin) pattern is similar to that of lacrimal and accessory lacrimal gland duct elements {19843013} and also sweat glands {19032382}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>The histopathological differential diagnosis includes oncocytic mucoepidermoid carcinoma, secretory carcinoma, acinic cell carcinoma, apocrine cystadenocarcinoma/carcinoma. Characteristic oncocytic cytomorphological features combined with the absence of nuclear pleomorphism, mitotic figures, and infiltrative margin favour oncocytoma (see also <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/65/68\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Apocrine carcinoma</em>; <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/65/141\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Secretory carcinoma</em>; <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/65/142\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Mucoepidermoid carcinoma of the lacrimal gland</em>).</p>\r\n<p>The clinical differential diagnosis includes melanoma {29344489}, sebaceous hyperplasia {23629804}, papilloma, and conjunctival cyst.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:57:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 979,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 744,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137013,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 744,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The cytology of caruncular/conjunctival oncocytoma has not been documented.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:57:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
